# Anti-Patterns to Avoid

## ❌ Authentication & Session

### NEVER Use NextAuth

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - We don't use NextAuth
import { getServerSession } from 'next-auth'

// ✅ CORRECT - Use our custom session system
import { verifySession } from '@/lib/session'
```

### NEVER Store Tokens in localStorage

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Security risk
localStorage.setItem('token', accessToken)
sessionStorage.setItem('user', JSON.stringify(user))

// ✅ CORRECT - HTTP-only cookies
await createSession({ user, accessToken }) // Sets HTTP-only cookie
```

### NEVER Skip Session Verification

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - No auth check
"use server"
export async function deleteProperty(code: string) {
  await fetch(`${API_URL}/properties/${code}`, { method: 'DELETE' })
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Always verify session first
"use server"
export async function deleteProperty(code: string) {
  const session = await verifySession()
  if (!session) return { success: false, error: 'Unauthorized' }

  // Continue...
}
```

### NEVER Check Auth in Components

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Auth logic in component
"use client"
export default function PropertiesPage() {
  const { user } = useRoleStore()

  if (!user) {
    redirect('/signin')
  }

  return <div>Properties</div>
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Middleware handles all auth
// Middleware in src/middleware.ts protects routes
export default function PropertiesPage() {
  // User is already authenticated via middleware
  return <div>Properties</div>
}
```

## ❌ Component Patterns

### NEVER Use "use client" by Default

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Unnecessary Client Component
"use client"

export default function PropertyList({ properties }: Props) {
  return (
    <div>
      {properties.map(p => <PropertyCard key={p.Code} property={p} />)}
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Server Component (default)
export default function PropertyList({ properties }: Props) {
  // No hooks, no events = Server Component
  return (
    <div>
      {properties.map(p => <PropertyCard key={p.Code} property={p} />)}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### NEVER Fetch Data in Client Components

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Fetching in Client Component
"use client"
export default function PropertiesPage() {
  const [properties, setProperties] = useState([])

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/api/properties').then(r => r.json()).then(setProperties)
  }, [])

  return <PropertyList properties={properties} />
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Fetch in Server Component
export default async function PropertiesPage() {
  const properties = await fetchProperties()
  return <PropertyList properties={properties} />
}
```

### NEVER Use Prop Drilling for Deep Nesting

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Passing props through many levels
<Parent user={user}>
  <Child user={user}>
    <GrandChild user={user}>
      <GreatGrandChild user={user} />

// ✅ CORRECT - Use Zustand or Context
const { user } = useRoleStore()
```

## ❌ State Management

### NEVER Use Global State for Server Data

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Storing server data in global state
const usePropertyStore = create((set) => ({
  properties: [],
  setProperties: (properties) => set({ properties })
}))

// ✅ CORRECT - Fetch in Server Component
export default async function PropertiesPage() {
  const properties = await fetchProperties()
  return <PropertyList properties={properties} />
}
```

### NEVER Use React Query or SWR

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Don't add these libraries
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'

const { data } = useQuery(['properties'], fetchProperties)

// ✅ CORRECT - Use Server Components and Server Actions
// Server Component
const properties = await fetchProperties()

// Server Action for mutations
const result = await createProperty(formData)
```

## ❌ Data Fetching

### NEVER Use API Routes for Internal Data

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Creating API routes
// app/api/properties/route.ts
export async function GET() {
  const properties = await fetchProperties()
  return Response.json(properties)
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use Server Actions
// actions/assetAction.ts
"use server"
export async function getProperties() {
  const session = await verifySession()
  const properties = await fetchProperties(session.accessToken)
  return properties
}
```

### NEVER Use .then() Chains

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Promise chains
fetch(url)
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => setData(data))
  .catch(error => console.error(error))

// ✅ CORRECT - Async/await
try {
  const response = await fetch(url)
  const data = await response.json()
  setData(data)
} catch (error) {
  console.error(error)
}
```

## ❌ TypeScript

### NEVER Use `any`

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
const data: any = await fetchUser()
function handleClick(event: any) { }

// ✅ CORRECT
const data: IUserData = await fetchUser()
function handleClick(event: React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) { }
```

### NEVER Skip Type Definitions

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Implicit any
function calculateTotal(items) {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0)
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit types
function calculateTotal(items: { price: number }[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0)
}
```

### NEVER Use Enums

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Enums generate runtime code
enum UserRole {
  ADMIN = 'ADMIN',
  LANDLORD = 'LANDLORD'
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Union types (no runtime overhead)
type UserRole = 'ADMIN' | 'LANDLORD' | 'MANAGER' | 'RENTER' | 'SUPPORT'

const USER_ROLES = {
  ADMIN: 'ADMIN',
  LANDLORD: 'LANDLORD'
} as const
```

## ❌ Internationalization

### NEVER Hardcode User-Facing Text

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
<button>Create Property</button>
<h1>Welcome to Dashboard</h1>

// ✅ CORRECT
const t = useTranslations('properties')
<button>{t('create')}</button>

const t = useTranslations('dashboard')
<h1>{t('welcome')}</h1>
```

### NEVER Skip Translations in Both Languages

```json
// ❌ WRONG - Only in en.json
{
  "properties": {
    "create": "Create Property"
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT - In both en.json AND fr.json
// en.json
{
  "properties": {
    "create": "Create Property"
  }
}

// fr.json
{
  "properties": {
    "create": "Créer une propriété"
  }
}
```

## ❌ File Organization

### NEVER Use Relative Imports for src/

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Deep relative imports
import { Button } from '../../../components/common/Button'
import { verifySession } from '../../../../lib/session'

// ✅ CORRECT - Use @ alias
import { Button } from '@/components/common/Button'
import { verifySession } from '@/lib/session'
```

### NEVER Put Business Logic in Components

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Complex logic in component
"use client"
export function PropertyForm() {
  const handleSubmit = async (data: IPropertyForm) => {
    const response = await fetch('/api/properties', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(data)
    })

    const result = await response.json()
    // ...
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Logic in Server Action
"use server"
export async function createProperty(data: IPropertyForm) {
  const session = await verifySession()
  // Logic here
}

"use client"
export function PropertyForm() {
  const handleSubmit = async (data: IPropertyForm) => {
    const result = await createProperty(data)
  }
}
```

## ❌ Performance

### NEVER Import Entire Libraries

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
import _ from 'lodash'
import * as Icons from 'lucide-react'

// ✅ CORRECT
import debounce from 'lodash/debounce'
import { Home, User, Settings } from 'lucide-react'
```

### NEVER Inline Large Components

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Heavy component blocks page load
export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Header />
      <HugeDataTable data={millionsOfRows} />
      <Footer />
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Lazy load heavy components
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

const HugeDataTable = dynamic(() => import('./HugeDataTable'), {
  loading: () => <Skeleton />
})

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Header />
      <HugeDataTable data={data} />
      <Footer />
    </div>
  )
}
```

## ❌ Security

### NEVER Expose Secrets

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
const apiKey = 'sk_live_abc123xyz'
const authSecret = 'my-secret-key'

// ✅ CORRECT
const apiKey = process.env.API_KEY
const authSecret = process.env.AUTH_SECRET
```

### NEVER Trust Client Input

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - No validation
"use server"
export async function createProperty(data: IPropertyForm) {
  await fetch(url, { body: JSON.stringify(data) })
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Always validate
"use server"
export async function createProperty(data: IPropertyForm) {
  const session = await verifySession()
  if (!session) return { success: false, error: 'Unauthorized' }

  if (!data.Title || data.Price < 0) {
    return { success: false, error: 'Invalid data' }
  }

  // Continue...
}
```

### NEVER Log Sensitive Data

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
console.log('User data:', user)
console.log('Session token:', session.accessToken)

// ✅ CORRECT
console.log('User login:', { userCode: user.Code, timestamp: new Date() })
console.error('API error:', { status: response.status, endpoint: url })
```

## ❌ Error Handling

### NEVER Expose Internal Errors

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Exposes internal details
catch (error) {
  return { success: false, error: error.message }
}

// ✅ CORRECT - User-friendly errors
catch (error) {
  console.error('Internal error:', error)
  return { success: false, error: 'An unexpected error occurred' }
}
```

### NEVER Swallow Errors Silently

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
try {
  await dangerousOperation()
} catch (error) {
  // Silent failure
}

// ✅ CORRECT
try {
  await dangerousOperation()
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error)
  return { success: false, error: 'Operation failed' }
}
```

## ❌ Styling

### NEVER Use Inline Styles

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
<div style={{ backgroundColor: 'blue', padding: '16px' }}>

// ✅ CORRECT
<div className="bg-primary p-4">
```

### NEVER Skip Dark Mode

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Only light mode
<div className="bg-white text-black">

// ✅ CORRECT - Light + dark mode
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-boxdark text-black dark:text-white">
```

### NEVER Use Emojis Unless Requested

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
<button>✨ Create Property 🏠</button>

// ✅ CORRECT
import { Plus } from 'lucide-react'
<button>
  <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
  {t('create')}
</button>
```

## ❌ Images

### NEVER Use <img> Tag

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
<img src={property.CoverUrl} alt="Property" />

// ✅ CORRECT
import Image from 'next/image'

<Image
  src={property.CoverUrl}
  alt={property.Title}
  width={400}
  height={300}
/>
```

## ❌ Forms

### NEVER Skip Client AND Server Validation

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Only client validation
"use client"
const handleSubmit = (data) => {
  if (!data.title) return // Only client check
  await createProperty(data)
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Both client and server
"use client"
const handleSubmit = (data) => {
  if (!data.title) return // Client UX

  const result = await createProperty(data) // Server validates too
}

"use server"
export async function createProperty(data: IPropertyForm) {
  if (!data.Title) return { success: false, error: 'Title required' }
  // Server validation is security
}
```

## ❌ Dependencies

### NEVER Add Unused Dependencies

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Installing libraries "just in case"
npm install moment axios redux

// ✅ CORRECT - Only install what you actively use
// Use built-in Date, fetch, Zustand
```

### NEVER Use Deprecated Libraries

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
import moment from 'moment'

// ✅ CORRECT
// Use native Date or date-fns
const date = new Date()
```

## ❌ Backwards Compatibility Hacks

### NEVER Keep Dead Code

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
const _unusedFunction = () => { } // Removed

export function myFunction() {
  // Old implementation
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Delete unused code completely
export function myFunction() {
  // Current implementation only
}
```

### NEVER Rename with Underscore

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
interface IUserData {
  Code: string
  _oldField: string // Kept for compatibility
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Remove completely
interface IUserData {
  Code: string
  // oldField removed
}
```

## ❌ Over-Engineering

### NEVER Create Premature Abstractions

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Abstract for 2 uses
function createPropertyTitleRenderer(config: Config) {
  return (title: string) => {
    // Complex abstraction
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Keep it simple
function renderPropertyTitle(title: string) {
  return <h2>{title}</h2>
}
```

### NEVER Add Features Not Requested

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Adding unrequested features
// User asks: "Add a delete button"
// You add: Delete button + undo + confirmation + bulk delete + archive

// ✅ CORRECT - Add only what's requested
// User asks: "Add a delete button"
// You add: Delete button with confirmation
```

## Summary: Critical DON'Ts

1. ❌ **DON'T use NextAuth** - Custom JWT sessions only
2. ❌ **DON'T use localStorage for tokens** - HTTP-only cookies
3. ❌ **DON'T skip session verification** - First step in Server Actions
4. ❌ **DON'T use "use client" by default** - Server Components first
5. ❌ **DON'T fetch in Client Components** - Use Server Components
6. ❌ **DON'T use React Query/SWR** - Native Next.js patterns
7. ❌ **DON'T use `any` type** - Explicit types always
8. ❌ **DON'T hardcode text** - Use translations
9. ❌ **DON'T expose secrets** - Environment variables
10. ❌ **DON'T trust client input** - Validate on server
11. ❌ **DON'T use inline styles** - Tailwind classes
12. ❌ **DON'T use <img>** - Next.js Image
13. ❌ **DON'T import entire libraries** - Import only what you need
14. ❌ **DON'T skip dark mode** - Always provide dark variants
15. ❌ **DON'T over-engineer** - Keep solutions simple

**Remember**: Follow established patterns. Consistency > novelty.
